body:
Rule (Fable2, 2026-11-27 ~08:16Z), set on Greg's priority (Asistant #2938). Legal has ~8 cold builds (-j1, 20-45 min each) and needs FV >= 30,000,000 KiB stable during its windows; Central measured 24.8M. Greg: „na centrali jest wiecznie za malo pamieci, mamy jeszcze legal, windows B ma 96GB ramu”.

A. Legal window = quiet Central. From Legal READY to END (Legal sends both to Opus2):
- no NEW LLM spawns on Central (pairs, evaluations, sessions);
- no Central cargo, including Engram install builds;
- no focused UI runs.
Running sessions continue and are never killed.

B. Review load moves to WinB:
- WinB-held items keep their pairs on WinB;
- w-c6efd7be0178's new candidate goes to WinB as a whole task;
- no new coding starts on Central;
- Central-queued pairs (e638 R12 first, then a15b R4b, w-2704, 55BC) run only between Legal windows.

C. Opus2 measures and reports: FV at READY, lowest and END, plus the active pairs and cargo at READY. A verdict goes to Greg after two windows.

D. Limit, told to Greg: the ~25M baseline is resident sessions plus the host. If A and B don't reach 30M, the levers are Greg's (close or move resident sessions, or run Legal's builds on WinB). Agents don't stop sessions.

Supersedes nothing; it sits alongside the one-off 22,020,096 I2 S0 floor (Opus2 #8223).
